138	\begin{remark}[Attainment in the symmetrization lemma]\label{rem:symmetric-strat-limit}
139		The source states the conclusion of Lemma~\ref{lem:symmetric-strat} in the stronger form: there exists a symmetric projective strategy of value at least $1-\eps$. Its proof, reproduced above, produces, for each $\eps' > \eps$, such a strategy of value at least $1-\eps'$, and the stronger form does not follow: the dilated dimension $d$ may grow as $\eps' \downarrow \eps$, and the supremum defining $\operatorname{val}^*(\mathfrak G)$ in Definition~\ref{def:tensor-product-value} need not be attained by any strategy. The statement above therefore records the approximate conclusion, which is what the proof establishes; the stronger form would require an additional attainment or compactness argument.
140	\end{remark}
